# Input field borders

Every standalone text input, select, textarea, and search field must show a visible border. Fields sit on `bg-white` or `bg-slate-50`, so a white, translucent, or `slate-200` border looks like no border.

## Required

```tsx
<Input className="border border-slate-300" />
<SelectTrigger className="border border-slate-300" />
<Textarea className="border border-slate-300" />
<SearchField /> // wrapper already includes border border-slate-300
```

- Resting: `border border-slate-300` (`#cbd5e1`) — stronger than card `slate-200` so fields read as inputs
- Hover: `hover:border-blue-300`
- Focus: `focus-visible:border-[#078FAB]`
- Shared class `.glass-form-control` already sets this slate-300 border; do not override it to white, transparent, or `slate-200`

## Forbidden on a standalone field

```tsx
<Input className="border-none" />
<Input className="border-0" />
<Input className="border-white/50" />
<Input className="border-slate-200" />
```

`border-0` is allowed only on an inner control whose parent already has the visible border (the inner `Input` inside `SearchField`).

`.shad-input` is `border-none` on purpose when it lives inside `.shad-form-item`, which already has `border border-light-300`. Do not use `.shad-input` as a standalone field.
